## Overview

Warps is a personal video project where I explored form and motion in 3D. I modelled, lit and animated the scenes in Blender, then edited the shots together in Premiere Pro. These are still frames from the video, in roughly the order they appear. I had no brief or client, so the only goal was to see how far simple shapes and materials could go once they started moving.

## Forms and materials

Each shot centres on a single object or material: a soft clay-like shape, two glass discs, a marble sphere in an arch, an iceberg on dark water, and a pixelated totem in an ice cave. I kept the backgrounds plain and the palette pastel so the materials do most of the work.

